+	 * D3 may not come back at all until the machine is rebooted. So keep it
+	 * to the device it was measured on: AR928X, 168c:002a.
+	 */
+	/*
+	 * Once per boot, and only after restoring config space by hand.
+	 *
+	 * As first written this could not work, and on 2026-08-25 it was caught
+	 * doing the opposite of recovery: it fired, and everything from there to
+	 * the reboot is "bb hang detected (0x4), resetting" over and over. The
+	 * adapter never came back -- twice in one day, each time taking the
+	 * network out for the rest of the session.
+	 *
+	 * Haiku's pci_set_powerstate() is not FreeBSD's. It writes the PMCSR and
+	 * returns (src/libs/compat/freebsd_network/pci.cpp): there is no
+	 * pci_cfg_save()/pci_cfg_restore() around the transition the way newbus
